    {
      "id": "b1a1c0de-0015-4000-8000-000000000015",
      "name": "Architecture note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -260],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1000, "height": 300, "color": 7,
        "content": "## SmartRecruit · sequential chain with parallel workers and a verifier loop\n\n**n8n is the orchestrator** (fixed, replayable path). Each HTTP node calls one agent or tool of the SmartRecruit API.\n\n- Top branch: job offer → **Job Analysis Agent** (weighted requirements, ESCO normalization)\n- Bottom branch, once per CV: **multimodal reader** (text layer, or vision model for scans / columns) → anonymization → **CV Agent** → chunks indexed in Qdrant\n- Then per candidate: **Matching Agent** (RAG on the CV) → **Audit Agent** (quote check + LLM verifier, sends rejected claims back to Matching once) → report.\n\nEvery step's output is saved in data/runs/<run_id>/ (audit trail). The AI recommends, the recruiter decides."
      }
    }
